# SRG-APP-000815-WSR-000160  -  CAT II
# The web server must require users to be individually authenticated before
# granting access to the shared accounts or resources.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000815-WSR-000160
group:           V-264342
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-004045
control_rev5:    IA-2

contribution:    Splunk Web keeps no credential store of its own: it authenticates through
                 the same authentication.conf [authentication] authType system as splunkd,
                 and web.conf [settings] offers no anonymous or unauthenticated access mode
                 to turn off. The application's share is therefore that an authentication
                 system is in force and that shared resources are reached through role
                 membership (authorize.conf [role_<roleName>]) rather than a shared login.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.

check:           authentication.conf [authentication] authType non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          authentication.conf [authentication] authType https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Issuance of an individual account per person and the prohibition on shared
                 credentials - carried by organizational account management.
external:        Where authType is LDAP, SAML, or ProxySSO, the web tier's individual
                 authentication is performed by the directory service or identity provider.
external:        Session handling in front of Splunk Web, where a reverse proxy or SSO
                 proxy is deployed - carried by that component.
external:        Whether role sharing in authorize.conf grants more than a person's duties
                 require - an organizational access-control determination.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:30;
                 splunk-spec-files/web.conf.spec:16 ([settings], no anonymous-access
                 setting); splunk-spec-files/authorize.conf.spec:67
finding:         Splunk Web does not require an individual authentication before granting
                 access to shared roles and knowledge objects because no authentication
                 system is in force (authentication.conf [authentication] authType is
                 empty); this determination is from the perspective of the application
                 layer alone.
